6. What are SCD Types (0–6)?

✅ SCD Type 1 — Overwrite old data

UPDATE dim_customer
SET address = new_address

✅ SCD Type 2 — Historical versioning

Create a new row when data changes.

Columns:

surrogate_key

start_date

end_date

is_active


PySpark example:

changed = new.alias("n").join(old.alias("o"), "cust_id") \
    .filter("n.address != o.address")

✅ SCD Type 3 — Add new column for previous value

Keeps only limited history EX:

previous_address
current_address

✅ SCD Type 6 — Hybrid (1 + 2 + 3)

Most advanced.


